= Portfolio and Project Management Institute (PPMI) Framework
\

== Project Management

Project management is the process of planning, organizing, executing, and controlling a specific project to achieve its objectives within time, cost, and quality constraints.

*Key Points:*
- Focuses on a single project.
- Ensures timely completion of project tasks and deliverables.
- Involves planning, monitoring, risk management, and resource allocation.

== Portfolio 
A portfolio is a collection of projects, programs, and processes managed together to achieve the strategic objectives of an organization. A project has a specific goal or objective to achieve, while a portfolio focuses on managing projects according to the organization’s overall strategic plan.

*Objectives of Portfolio:*
+ Align projects and programs with organizational goals.
+ Use resources (time, money, and people) effectively.
+ Balance risks and returns across different projects.
+ Monitor overall progress and performance.
+ Support decision-making for future investments and priorities.

== Project Portfolio Management (PPM)
Project Portfolio Management (PPM) is the process of managing a group of projects together to achieve the organization’s goals. It helps to choose the right projects, use resources properly, manage risks, and get maximum benefit from all projects. It is usually done by portfolio managers or a Project Management Office (PMO).

*Key Points:*
- Focuses on a collection of projects.
- Helps projects provide maximum value to the organization.
- Involves selecting, prioritizing, and monitoring projects.
- Helps manage resources, costs, risks, and performance.

== Importance of Project Portfolio Management
+ Better Planning: Helps select projects that give better results.
+ Risk and Reward: Helps identify projects with high risk and high benefit.
+ Overall View: Gives a complete picture of all projects.
+ Financial Management: Helps manage money properly.
+ Better Decisions: Helps managers make better project decisions.
+ Reduces Cost: Avoids unnecessary expenses and improves efficiency.
+ Monitors Progress: Helps track the progress of all projects.
+ Achieves Goals: Helps the organization achieve its overall objectives.

